    "title": "Actor Bill Murray at UConn's NCAA Tournament games",
    "text": "PHILADELPHIA, PENNSYLVANIA - MARCH 22: Actor Bill Murray in the stands during game between UCLA Bruins and UConn Huskies in the second half in the second round of the 2026 NCAA Men's Basketball Tournament held at Xfinity Mobile Arena on March 22, 2026 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. (Photo by Ben Solomon/NCAA Photos via Getty Images)Ben Solomon/NCAA Photos via Getty ImagesLegendary actor and comedian Bill Murray is in attendance for the UConn men's basketball team's Round of 32 matchup with UCLA in the NCAA Tournament Sunday in Philadelphia.Murray was seated a couple rows behind the UConn bench, where his son Luke serves as an assistant coach under Dan Hurley. He also attended the Huskies' opening round victory over Furman from Xfinity Mobile Arena.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢The 75-year-old actor got his start on Saturday Night Live in the late 1970s and ultimately won two Primetime Emmy Awards and a Golden Globe across his successful entertainment career. Murray famously starred in \"Caddyshack\" and the \"Ghostbusters\" series and frequently collaborates with famed director Wes Anderson.Bill Murray watches during the first half between UConn and Furman in the first round of the NCAA college basketball tournament, Friday, March 20, 2026, in Philadelphia. (AP Photo/Matt Slocum)Matt Slocum/APLuke was raised in Palisades, N.Y. and has maintained deep ties to the Nutmeg State beyond his current stint at UConn. He was a two-sport athlete at St. Luke's School in New Canaan and enrolled at Fairfield University while he coached several AAU programs. His first collegiate coaching gig was offered by current Huskies general manager Tom Moore at Quinnipiac, where Murray served as the Bobcats' Director of Basketball Operations.More For YouWith Hurley hiring Luke to his staff in 2021, Murray became a regular presence at UConn basketball games. Luke has recently been listed as a leading contender for the Boston College head coaching positionArticle continues below this adCT Insider LogoGet daily updates from the UConn basketball world.March 22, 2026|Updated March 22, 2026 10:46 p.m.Trending Reporter/Audience ProducerDeclan Walsh is a Trending Reporter and Audience Producer at Hearst Connecticut, focusing on trending topics, lifestyle and sports. Originally from New Jersey, Declan studied Journalism-Sports Media at the University of Florida. He previously covered women's basketball at NCAA.com and made stops at Sports Illustrated, FOX Sports and The Palm Beach Post.",
